    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but it's still a hard sell for them. they see the money just \"vanishing\" from the books. is there any way to describe the way value erodes over time using a more... i don't know, vivid or relatable analogy? something that makes the concept of an asset slowly losing its worth feel less like an abstract math rule and more like a natural process?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
