      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A relatable analogy is the way a sturdy, well-made wooden bridge slowly succumbs to the elements, like rain and time. You can tell them that the machine, much like that bridge, is being used up by the constant demands of production—the wear and tear from grinding and running. The depreciation is simply the accounting way of saying that the bridge, or the CNC machine, is slowly being used up by its life cycle. It's not that the machine is broken, but that its *ability* to function at its peak efficiency is gradually diminishing.",
      "source": "target",
